[00:09.12]
[00:15.29]Flocks of seagulls feather the sky
[00:20.20]Too, with ease, my sandwich they bite
[00:25.30]Papers and keyboard are not what I like
[00:30.30]So, you see, I'm strolling for joy
[00:34.92]
[00:35.24]Where the nature thrives has always nourished my life
[00:40.41]Of it all I cannot wait to sing you a slice
[00:46.07]
[00:46.35]The waves combing beaches and the footprints sun-baked
[00:51.42]Or meadows lushly greening forth the vibrance for a change
[00:56.33]To play with, no mistaking, all the creatures She made
[01:01.36]For everything alive I meet is just so loveable my mate
[01:09.29]
[01:16.57]Have would you not but a savory cup?
[01:21.60]Vibe round the block tells you it's a must
[01:26.50]Not that the koalas, nor possums, like us,
[01:31.48]are into the flavor of coffee——but buds
